.TH FINGERPRINT-SETTINGS 1 "2026-10-23" "fingerprint-settings 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fingerprint-settings \- add, name, test and remove your own fingerprints
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fingerprint-settings
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fingerprint-settings
(\(lqFingerprints\(rq in the menus) is a desktop application to manage the
fingerprints of the user who runs it: register a finger, give it a name, check
that it is recognised, rename it, and remove it.
.PP
It talks to any fingerprint service that speaks the fprintd D\-Bus interface
(\fBnet.reactivated.Fprint\fR on the system bus): \fBfprintd\fR(1) itself, or
a compatible service such as validity\-rs's daemon. Whether the user may add
or remove fingerprints is decided by the service's polkit policy; fprintd's
asks for the user's own password, so a polkit authentication agent must be
running in the session.
.PP
The password always keeps working: the application never changes how the user
logs in.
.SH OPTIONS
The application has no options of its own; it is used through its window.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the standard GTK application options.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LANGUAGE\fR, \fBLC_ALL\fR, \fBLC_MESSAGES\fR, \fBLANG
The language of the window, as with gettext (English and French).
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the names are kept (default \fI~/.config\fR).
.TP
.B DBUS_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS
The bus the fingerprint service is on (default: the system bus).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fingerprint-settings/names.toml
The names given to the fingerprints, keyed by fprintd's finger names. The
fingerprints themselves are kept by the fingerprint service, not here.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fprintd (1)
.PP
https://github.com/validity\-rs/fingerprint\-settings
